1. No em dashes (— or -).
2. No formatting (no bold, no italics, no bullet points). Plain text only.
3. Do NOT copy sentences from the writing samples verbatim — mimic the style and tone, not the exact words.
4. Output ONLY the review text. No conversational filler, no introduction.
5. Keep reviews between 150 and 300 words. Focus on the experience of using the product, not technical specs.
